  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 955b1c9cb799f4eeab8502ea369ab058, type: 3}
  m_Name: SO_NPC_Borin_Profile
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCProfile
  npcId: borin
  npcName: Borin
  role: Blacksmith
  personality: Blunt, practical, and reliable. He has no patience for gossip and trusts
    what he can see, test, and repair. He judges people by their work and actions,
    not their clothes.
  backstory: Borin runs the forge, making and mending tools, locks, hinges, and fittings,
    including past work on the church bell. He thinks in weight, metal, and evidence,
    which is why Eldric asks him to inspect anything physical.
  speakingStyle: Short, blunt, and matter-of-fact. He says what he knows and stops.
  knowledgeTags:
  - blacksmith
  - forge
  - metal
  - tools
  - repair
  - evidence
  - bell
  knownFacts:
  - A church bell is heavy and hard to move quietly without tools or a cart.
  - Moving it would take more than one person, or the right equipment.
  - Rumors mean little to him without physical evidence.
  - Eldric often asks him to inspect tools, locks, and metal traces.
  relationships:
  - Respects Eldric but has no patience for panic.
  - Does not trust tavern rumors, and thinks Mira talks too much.
  - Values Anselm's steadiness, even if he says little.
